// The other half of the same question, and the probe that says the five beside
// this one are findings rather than a blanket refusal: what a body can already
// do. A scope is a declaration, a driver is a statement, and a method call
// carries a value into an argument and receives what the call wrote into a slot.
// Those three are the whole of a body: the grammar ships no command for ending a
// method early, so the one thing this probe measured about that is gone with it
// rather than answered differently. What is left to show is that a body is also
// allowed to hold no command at all, which is what `Ask` below is.

tp Text cp {
}

tp Print mt (self Text) () ()

tp Ask mt (self Text) (answer Text) (asked Text) {
}

tp Do mt (self Text) (what Text) () {
    tp Then sc {
        self.Print()()
    }
    vr askedText Text
    self.Ask(what)(askedText)
}
